 previous fix (","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"ReducerStoreRegistry"},{"text":") sidestepped this with a","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"single root-injected registry keyed by ","type":"text"},{"type":"emphasis","inlineContent":[{"text":"concrete Store type","type":"text"}]},{"text":" — which has a real, documented","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"weakness: two simultaneous instances of the same reducer type at different tree positions","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"collide, since the registry has no notion of tree position, only type.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"ReducerKeyPath"},{"text":" fixes this by construction: it’s a position in the tree, built by composing","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"one hop at a time from the true root (injected exactly once, above everything, via","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"ReducerStoreView"},{"text":"\/","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":".environmentObject(store)"},{"type":"text","text":"), carried explicitly through ordinary "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"init"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"parameters rather than resolved from a global. Composing via closures (not Swift’s native","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"KeyPath.appending(path:)"},{"type":"text","text":", which requires decomposing an already-composed KeyPath — something"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"Swift provides no API for) means each "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":".append(_:)"},{"type":"text","text":" call captures the previous resolver"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"directly, with no information loss."}]},{"type":"heading","text":"Usage","level":2,"anchor":"Usage"},{"type":"codeListing","code":["struct ChildView: View {","    let model: ChildReducer.State","    let send: (ChildReducer.When